---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<section id="features" class="relative scroll-mt-24 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="max-w-3xl" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">The complete model, without the platform</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.03em] text-white sm:text-[2.9rem]">
        Everything between “send a message”<br class="hidden sm:block" />{" "}
        <span class="text-muted">and “it actually happened”.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-pretty text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Snodra is not a broker and not a framework you rewrite your services around. It is the
        missing layer that makes commands, events and long-running processes consistent — with your
        stores, your languages and your deployment.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-6">
      <article
        class="panel card-hover relative overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-4"
        data-reveal
        style="--reveal-delay: 30ms"
      >
        <div class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-24 -top-24 h-64 w-64 rounded-full bg-primary/15 blur-3xl"></div>
        <div class="relative">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="radio" size={18} /></span>
            <p class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-primary-soft">Routing</p>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Route to the live handler, not a queue.</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-lg text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
            Services register the command and query types they handle. A sender asks for a type and
            gets whichever instance is live. Deadlines, retries, priority, streaming and
            subscription queries are enforced once, at the router.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3">
            {
              [
                ["command", "one handler · one reply"],
                ["query", "one, many, or a stream"],
                ["no handler", "fails fast · never queued"],
              ].map(([title, detail]) => (
                <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-black/20 px-3 py-2.5">
                  <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] text-primary-soft">{title}</p>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-[0.72rem] text-dim">{detail}</p>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel card-hover overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="database" size={18} /></span>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">No dual writes.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Events are published through the outbox in the same transaction as your state change. A
          relay publishes them; processors dedupe with markers in the same store.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg border border-line bg-black/25 px-3 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.62rem] leading-relaxed text-dim">
          <span class="text-teal">BEGIN</span><br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;update order<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;insert into outbox<br />
          <span class="text-teal">COMMIT</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel card-hover overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 30ms">
        <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="clock" size={18} /></span>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Sagas, not workflow engines.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Long-running processes with associations, deadlines and a relay that retries commands.
          State lives in your message store; no extra service to run.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 rounded-lg border border-line bg-black/20 px-3 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.62rem] leading-relaxed text-dim">
          <p><span class="text-pink">OrderPlaced</span> <span class="text-dim">→</span> reserve stock</p>
          <p><span class="text-amber">deadline 30s</span> <span class="text-dim">→</span> release stock</p>
          <p><span class="text-teal">PaymentFailed</span> <span class="text-dim">→</span> compensate</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel card-hover overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-4" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="layers" size={18} /></span>
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-primary-soft">Stores are add-ons</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Your events and state stay yours.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-lg text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Choose one event store and one message store per service. Swap them without rewriting the
          service, and test against in-memory stores without containers.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-black/20 p-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-dim">Event store</p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
              <span class="chip">Kafka</span><span class="chip">RabbitMQ Streams</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-black/20 p-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-dim">Message store</p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
              <span class="chip">MongoDB</span><span class="chip">PostgreSQL</span><span class="chip">MySQL</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel card-hover overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-3" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 30ms">
        <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="key" size={18} /></span>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Security is in the contract.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Anonymous, static token, OIDC/JWT or mTLS — with per-service ACLs and the caller's identity
          forwarded through handlers.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
          <span class="chip">mTLS</span><span class="chip">JWT</span><span class="chip">ACL</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel card-hover overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-3" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="activity" size={18} /></span>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">See the system, not guesses.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Topology, queue depth, processor lag, dead letters and the schema catalogue in the dashboard; OTLP metrics for the
          dashboards you already have.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
          <span class="chip">OpenTelemetry</span><span class="chip">Dashboard</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article
        class="panel card-hover relative overflow-hidden p-6 md:col-span-6"
        data-reveal
        style="--reveal-delay: 30ms"
      >
        <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-0 w-1/2 bg-gradient-to-l from-teal/10 to-transparent"></div>
        <div class="relative flex flex-col gap-6 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:justify-between">
          <div class="max-w-2xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="icon-box"><Icon name="check" size={18} /></span>
              <p class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-primary-soft">Interoperability</p>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">One protocol. Proven, not promised.</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
              The conformance runner checks a client against a real server and fake hubs, with PASS,
              FAIL, SKIPPED or NOT IMPLEMENTED per check id. A Kotlin service and a Rust service are
              indistinguishable in front of the server and on the event store.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-3">
            <div class="flex -space-x-2">
              <span class="grid h-10 w-10 place-items-center rounded-full border border-line bg-panel text-[0.62rem] font-semibold text-pink">Kt</span>
              <span class="grid h-10 w-10 place-items-center rounded-full border border-line bg-panel text-[0.62rem] font-semibold text-teal">Rs</span>
              <span class="grid h-10 w-10 place-items-center rounded-full border border-dashed border-line bg-panel text-[0.62rem] font-semibold text-dim">Py</span>
              <span class="grid h-10 w-10 place-items-center rounded-full border border-teal/40 bg-teal/10 text-[0.62rem] font-semibold text-teal">Go</span>
            </div>
            <a href="/docs/concepts/" class="btn btn-ghost !min-h-9 !px-3.5 !py-2 !text-[0.8rem]">
              The model
              <Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
